sequenceDiagram
autonumber
participant G as Caller
participant A as AbilitySystemComponent
participant S as AbilitySpec
participant K as AbilitySpecContainer
participant P as AbilityProxy
participant W as ProcessWorld of the caster
participant R as TaskSequenceRuntime
participant T as Task
participant X as Target
G->>A: TryActivateAbility(Ability, Tag or request)
Note over G,A: also triggers, the input buffer and ActivateImmediateAbilities
A->>A: AbilityDataPacket.GenerateFrom(spec, request, ...)
A->>S: SourceRefusal: tags, crowd control, rules, CanStart
A->>A: level zero, while-active, Blocks, ChanceToActivate
alt refused
A-->>G: a Refused ActivationResult, OnAbilityRefused(ActivationRefusal)
end
A->>A: CancelAbilitiesCancelledBy
alt the request CancelsTargeting, as a press does, not a trigger or an activation at start
A->>A: YieldTargetingTo: another ability still choosing its target gives way where its While Targeting yields, cancelled, nothing paid, its claim let go
end
A->>A: then the activation policy
A->>K: ActivateAbility(data)
K->>A: ClaimActive: OnAbilityActivate, components Start
K->>P: TakeProxy, or GenerateProxy, which compiles
K->>P: ActivateTargetingTask(token, data)
P->>W: Register(CompiledTargeting).HandledBy(caster).With(data).In(world).Run()
W->>T: the targeting task's Prepare, Activate, Clean
T-->>W: TARGET packets through SetTargetingPacket
W-->>P: relay.WhenTerminated
K->>S: PickRefusal: a component's CanTakeTarget, as Cast Range's
K->>K: ResolveTarget(ImplicitTag) into TARGET_REAL
K->>S: TargetRefusal(target, data), the target checks
alt targeting cancelled or failed, or its pick or target refused
K-->>A: the activation ends Cancelled, nothing paid, a refused pick or target told through OnAbilityRefused
end
K->>K: WindUp: its entity's and its components' wind-ups, as Turn To Face
K->>S: ApplyUsageEffects(data), unless a stage takes it
Note over K,S: a component's ApplyUsage in their place, as Toggle's, else a cooldown or a charge through its CooldownModel, the Cost effect, the attribute costs
K->>K: components Commit, CompileGrantedTags()
Note over K,P: The claim is released here, unless a stage is critical
K->>P: Activate(token, data)
P->>P: the asset loaders run inline
P->>W: Register(CompiledSequence).HandledBy(caster).With(data).In(world).Run()
W->>R: its TaskSequenceProcess runs the stages
loop each stage
R->>R: a Branch skips it when its AbilityStageCondition fails
R->>R: OnInit, OnAbilityStageActivate
R->>T: Prepare, Execute (task.Activate), Clean
T->>X: GenerateEffectSpec(data.EffectOrigin, effect)
T->>X: ApplyCarrier(spec)
R->>R: WhenAll or WhenAny, OnTerminate, OnAbilityStageEnd
end
W-->>P: relay.WhenTerminated
K->>A: CleanHandle: release the claim, EndActivation, OnAbilityEnd
K->>K: components End, the lent item's Used, CompileGrantedTags()
Note over A,R: Interrupts: Inject(InterruptSequenceInjection.Instance) cancels the run. CancelAbilitiesTask and CancelledBy spare critical stages
